  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 60000,
    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "Vendor 60 Gbps non-blocking fabric across 30 ports (30 x 1G = 30 Gbit/s each way); forwarding rate 44.64 Mpps, line rate."
  },
  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 1440,
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf",
    "note": "1,440 W only with both internal power supplies connected: the datasheet states 720 W with one PSU and 1,440 W with two. The 24 port ceilings sum to 24 x 90 W = 2,160 W, so even fully fed the budget is 720 W short of a full 90 W load and averages 60 W per port."
  },
  "notes": "M4250 series common platform: 16K MAC addresses, 4K ARP/NDP entries, 4K VLANs, static routes (894 IPv4 / 126 IPv6) plus RIP (32 IPv4), DHCP server (2K leases), sFlow, SNMP, console/telnet/SSH CLI and the AV web GUI. The 802.3bt member of the 26-port family; the port census is identical to the M4250-26G4F-PoE+ (24 PoE + 2 copper + 4 SFP), so the model string carries the SKU to keep the catalogue keys apart (modelKey() strips the plus signs that distinguish the two variants). Two fixed C14 inlets against the PoE+ model one, and the chassis is 143 mm deeper. Sources: datasheet https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf and https://kb.netgear.com/000064904/NETGEAR-AV-Line-of-Fully-Managed-Switches-M4250-Series."
